#
# Where things are on this machine. Copy to `paths.local` beside the scripts (git-ignored) and
# set your own paths; common.setting() reads it. An environment variable of the same name wins
# over the file -- the way to point a throwaway machine (a rented server) somewhere without
# writing a file. A name left out stays unset, and every tool then requires the option instead.
#
#   MIRROR_ROOT      the collection                     (--root)
#   PACK_WORK        b2-pack's flat working directory    (pack-progress.py --work)
#   PACK_TARGET      where the packed units are written  (tar-subtree.py --target-root)
#   VERIFY_SCRATCH   where a whole unit is unpacked      (rar-verify-content.py --scratch)

MIRROR_ROOT=D:\mirror
PACK_WORK=D:\work
PACK_TARGET=D:\packed
VERIFY_SCRATCH=D:\verify
